      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Validation Hole:** The validation checks that `offset` does not exceed `max_image_buffer_bytes`, but it does not verify that `offset` is bounded by the `size` of the frame itself. Since `offset` represents where the image data starts within the frame, an offset greater than the frame size is structurally invalid and could cause logic errors when consumers slice the buffer.\n\nPlease add an invariant check to enforce `offset \u003c\u003d size`:\n```cpp\n\t\tif (offset \u003e size) {\n\t\t\tCPRINTS(\"Error: Type %u image offset (%u) exceeds frame size (%u).\",\n\t\t\t\ttype, offset, size);\n\t\t\tgoto error_exit;\n\t\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8372808_8405f958-a188-4dc1-865d-7063f2d0c48b.pb)",
